<title>TURKEY: Turkey C/A deficit at $2.31 bln in Jan-June 1996.</title>
<headline>Turkey C/A deficit at $2.31 bln in Jan-June 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's current account balance showed a provisional deficit of $2.31 billion in January-June 1996, up sharply from $15 million in the first half of 1995, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The current account deficit was $2.34 billion in 1995, after a $2.63-billion surplus the previous year.</p>
<p>The release of foreign trade and current account data have been delayed due to technical problems caused by Turkey's customs union with the European Union since the start of 1996.</p>
<p>The central bank, which did not release current account tables for April and May, gave the following provisional figures for June 1996:</p>
<p>    ($ million)	    Jun96  Mar96  Jun95  Jan-Jun96 Jan-Jun95</p>
<p>Current account	    -223   -946     10    -2,314	  -15 </p>
<p>Exports fob		 1,824  2,030  1,871    11,041     10,128 </p>
<p>Imports fob		-3,234 -3,593 -3,018   -19,605    -13,045</p>
<p>Gold imports		  -91   -139   -123	-594	 -351</p>
<p>Foreign trade blnc     -1,410 -1,563 -1,147    -8,564     -4,917 </p>
<p>Invisible credit	  1,739  1,220  1,669     9,130	7,040</p>
<p>Tourism			 693    206    559     2,000	1,758</p>
<p>Invisible debit	    -846   -812   -973    -4,978     -4,598</p>
